      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white text-center">How Long to Keep Tattoo Consent Forms (Retention Period)</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">A signed consent and waiver is only useful if you can produce it years later — and most disputes or health-department inspections happen well after the appointment. Attorneys commonly recommend retaining signed forms for <strong class="text-white">at least seven years</strong>; some advise keeping them indefinitely for clients with complex health histories. A free printable form covers you today, but paper stacks get lost — if you ever move to digital signing, long-term storage becomes trivial and searchable.</p>
