      <p class="mt-4 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">For adult clients, a signed, dated form with photo-ID verification is generally sufficient — notarization isn't required. Notarization usually enters the picture only for <strong class="text-white">minors in states that mandate a notarized parental consent form</strong>. The process is straightforward: fill the form, meet a licensed notary public, present valid ID, and sign in their presence so they can apply the official seal. If you only serve adults, skip the notary and keep the signed printable form on file.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

